The Python 3.12 glibc wheels of psycopg-binary 3.3.6 also contain native
shared libraries under psycopg_binary.libs/. The license directory in those
wheels contains LICENSE.txt. License names for the native libraries are
recorded in reviews/MOSS-016/license-review.md from the wheel SBOM, strings
in the binaries, the psycopg 3.3.6 build scripts, upstream license files, and
RPM License tags. In short, for the wheels that match the published
linux/amd64 and linux/arm64 images:

  libpq (SONAME libpq.so.5.18; build pin PostgreSQL 18.6) — PostgreSQL License
    https://www.postgresql.org/about/licence/
  libssl and libcrypto from OpenSSL 3.5.8 — Apache License 2.0
    https://raw.githubusercontent.com/openssl/openssl/openssl-3.5.8/LICENSE.txt
  linux/arm64 also bundles OpenSSL 1.1.1k (libcrypto.so.1.1.1k), linked from
    the Kerberos libraries — OpenSSL License and original SSLeay license
    https://raw.githubusercontent.com/openssl/openssl/OpenSSL_1_1_1k/LICENSE
  libldap and liblber — build script pin OpenLDAP 2.6.14, OpenLDAP Public
    License Version 2.8
    https://raw.githubusercontent.com/openldap/openldap/OPENLDAP_REL_ENG_2_6_14/LICENSE
  krb5 libraries — MIT (RPM License tag)
  libcom_err — MIT (RPM License tag)
  PCRE 8.32 on linux/amd64, PCRE2 10.32 on linux/arm64 — BSD (RPM License tag)
  Cyrus SASL — BSD with advertising (RPM License tag)
  libselinux — Public Domain (RPM License tag)
  libkeyutils — RPM License tag "GPLv2+ and LGPLv2+"
  linux/arm64 libcrypt — libxcrypt 4.1.1, RPM License tag
    "LGPLv2+ and BSD and Public Domain"
  linux/amd64 libcrypt — license text was not in the wheel and no RPM
    License tag was attached by the wheel SBOM. License: unverified.

