PyPI publishes wheels for psycopg-binary 3.3.6 and no source distribution.
The C extension sources are in that git tag under psycopg_c. The wheel build
copies them with tools/ci/copy_to_binary.py.

The image build installs these wheels with uv sync and copies the virtualenv.
It does not copy this file. A later image change would have to place this
notice, the GPL text, and the bundled libraries' license texts into the image.
